{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2007-09-02T00:00:00+00:00", "id": "759562", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/759562?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/759562?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/759562?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/759562?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/759562?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/759562?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A759562"}, "updated": "2023-03-10T04:42:03.554711+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "76", "artid": "094013", "year": 2007, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Vogelsang, Werner"}, {"full_name": "Yuan, Feng"}], "texkeys": ["Vogelsang:2007jk"], "abstracts": [{"value": "We compare several recent theoretical studies of the single transverse spin asymmetry in dijet-correlations at hadron colliders. We show that the results of these studies are all consistent. To establish this, we investigate in particular the two-gluon exchange contributions to the relevant initial and final state interactions in the context of a simplifying model. Overall, the results confirm that the dijet imbalance obeys at best a non-standard or 'generalized' transverse-momentum-dependent factorization."}], "control_number": 759562, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.76.094013"}], "arxiv_eprints": [{"value": "0708.4398"}], "titles": [{"title": "Hadronic Dijet Imbalance and Transverse-Momentum Dependent Parton Distributions"}, {"title": "Hadronic Dijet Imbalance and Transverse-Momentum Dependent Parton Distributions"}], "author_count": 2, "document_type": ["article"]}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=eprint%200708.4398&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publ